course: dictionary
lesson: 13356
title: Handsomely: money, winning and fine things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Handsomely is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. Its main meaning is generously, in large amounts. «The farmer paid the helpers handsomely for their work.» The clue is paid: the helpers got a lot of money, more than just a little.
explain: Handsomely can also mean clearly, by a big margin, when someone wins. «The home team won handsomely, 6 goals to 1.» Winning by a lot is the clue. In stories it often means a big reward: «The brave knight was rewarded handsomely by the king.»
explain: Handsomely can mean in a fine, elegant way, for things that are finely dressed or made. «The queen was dressed handsomely for the feast.» When you meet handsomely, look at the words around it: money, winning, or fine clothes and things will show you which meaning fits.
fact: Handsomely is an adverb, so it tells you how an action is done.
fact: «Handsomely» means generously, in large amounts, as in «paid handsomely».
fact: «Handsomely» can mean clearly and by a big margin, as in «won handsomely».
fact: «Handsomely» can also mean in a fine, elegant way, as in «dressed handsomely».
exercise: The workers were «paid handsomely» for finishing the bridge early. What does handsomely mean here? | Slowly and sadly | Late in the evening | *Generously, with a large amount of money | Quietly, so nobody could hear
exercise: Our team «won handsomely», 6 goals to 0. What does won handsomely suggest? | They lost the game | *Clearly, by a big margin | They did not play at all | Narrowly, by just one point
exercise: The palace hall was decorated handsomely with gold and silk. Which meaning fits best? | Quietly, in the dark | *In a fine, elegant way | Roughly and carelessly | Sadly and slowly
test: The king rewarded the knight handsomely. What does handsomely mean? | *Given a large, generous reward | Sent away from the castle | Asked to leave the court | Given a small, plain prize
test: She was dressed handsomely for the wedding, in silk and gold. What does handsomely mean? | Sadly and slowly | *In a fine, elegant way | Quickly and noisily | Without any clothes
exam: What does handsomely mean in «The hero was handsomely rewarded by the king»? | *Generously, with a big reward | Slowly, like a snail | Badly, with no reward at all | Sadly, with tears
